 "analysis": [
  "1 of 6 key cells improved after Holm (4 required): mixed/16MiB/8Mbit 19.93 -> 15.86 s. Holm steps: mixed/16MiB/8Mbit p 0.0026 vs 0.0083; mixed/16MiB/60Mbit p 0.018 vs 0.0100; mixed/4MiB/8Mbit p 0.365 vs 0.0125 (stops at the second step).",
  "v1 to v2 per key cell (mean start time C0 -> CW): mixed/4MiB/8Mbit v1 12.37 -> 8.06, v2 9.86 -> 9.36; mixed/4MiB/30Mbit v1 15.14 -> 9.5, v2 11.01 -> 11.08; mixed/4MiB/60Mbit v1 15.93 -> 11.86, v2 13.2 -> 13.69; mixed/16MiB/8Mbit v1 16.91 -> 13.03, v2 19.93 -> 15.86; mixed/16MiB/30Mbit v1 17.83 -> 15.37, v2 17.21 -> 16.96; mixed/16MiB/60Mbit v1 18.25 -> 17.95, v2 19.77 -> 16.46. The 4 MiB cells, which carried v1's smallest p-values, show no difference in v2 (d 0.08, -0.01, -0.08); their v1 C0 means were higher and their CW means lower than in v2. The 16 MiB 8 and 60 Mbit/s cells keep a gain of 3-4 s; 16MiB/30Mbit does not. Within an arm the two series differ by up to 4.1 s (C0 mixed/16MiB/60Mbit 21.8 vs 17.7 s, series_means_s), in no common direction across cells; descriptive only.",
  "Descriptive shape (not a criterion): start times cluster at roughly 5 s steps in both arms. The watchdog removes part of the slowest tail (runs over 20 s, C0 vs CW: mixed/4MiB/8Mbit 4/0, mixed/4MiB/30Mbit 5/3, mixed/4MiB/60Mbit 7/6, mixed/16MiB/8Mbit 19/9, mixed/16MiB/30Mbit 14/13, mixed/16MiB/60Mbit 19/10), but in mixed/4MiB/30Mbit fewer runs land in the fastest cluster (<= 6 s: C0 19, CW 11), so the means meet. A hypothesis for this trade-off, not tested: a ban and re-request can cost a start that legacy would have finished from the fast peers anyway.",
  "Start-phase stall time (start.stall_s, a guard metric here, descriptive): the mean is lower with the watchdog in every cell where C0 stalls at all; the stalls are mostly shorter rather than fewer: mixed/16MiB/30Mbit 1.643 -> 0.038 s (runs with a stall 10 -> 6, unadjusted p 0.0002); mixed/16MiB/60Mbit 3.107 -> 1.605 s (runs with a stall 20 -> 25, unadjusted p 0.0289); mixed/1MiB/30Mbit 1.066 -> 0.429 s (runs with a stall 13 -> 10, unadjusted p 0.0217); mixed/4MiB/30Mbit 1.196 -> 0.248 s (runs with a stall 11 -> 13, unadjusted p 0.0058); mixed/4MiB/60Mbit 3.867 -> 2.737 s (runs with a stall 30 -> 31, unadjusted p 0.0852). This was not the registered primary metric and cannot pass the gate after the fact; it is a candidate hypothesis for a new version on new data.",
  "No guard regression after Holm over 28 tests; the mixed/1MiB/30Mbit guard cell (v1's descriptive flag) 9.727 -> 9.912 s, regression p 0.44. Hard checks pass: 0 bans in C0, every CW run in the bounded mixed cells within the limit (249/252 runs with a ban, 444 bans), 0 failed runs, 0 app tracebacks, 0 infrastructure retries. Check (a), no false bans without stalled peers, is carried from v1."
 ]
